# ResumeTailor — AI editor rules
# Full version: AI_RULES.md · Decisions: docs/memory.md · Design: docs/architecture.md

## What this is
Browser extension (MV3, Chrome/Firefox/Edge). One Structured Profile + one job
description -> one page of LaTeX. Users bring their own AI key and model.

## Invariants — never break
1. src/core/ is pure TS: no chrome.*/browser.*, no fetch, no DOM, no imports from
   providers/ ui/ background/ content/. Dependencies point inward only.
2. The AI never authors facts. It returns item IDs + rephrasings of text it was
   shown. Dates, employers, titles, contact and role notes are joined locally.
3. Role notes are USER-AUTHORED free text (Experience.note). Never author,
   default, suggest or hardcode note content anywhere. Rendered verbatim,
   never sent to a model, never dropped by a plan.
4. Profile item IDs (e1, e1b3, p2, s1) are permanent, never reused.
5. One error type: AppError with an ErrorCode and a hand-written userMessage.
   No bare `throw new Error()` outside core/types/errors.ts. No empty catch.
6. No backend, no telemetry. Only outbound request: the user's chosen provider.
7. One page mandatory. Overflow is surfaced with cuts, never silently truncated.

## Content
- Never invent a metric, technology or achievement not in the profile.
- Never commit a real person's name, employer, dates or circumstances. Public repo;
  fixtures use obviously-fictional companies.
- Every number/proper noun in a rewritten bullet must exist in its source bullet
  text or evidence, or the rewrite is rejected and the original is kept.
- Google XYZ shape for bullets: accomplished [X] measured by [Y] by doing [Z].
  Warn when missing; never block.

## Tokens (the user pays)
- Send IDs, not prose. Truncate the index to 90 chars per bullet.
- Rewrite only selected bullets. Heuristics before any model call.
- Cache by content hash. One call per tailoring. No streaming, no refine loops.

## Code
- TypeScript strict. No `any`; `unknown` at boundaries then narrow.
- SOLID/DRY/KISS. No interface with one implementation. No dependency for what
  20 lines can do — adding one requires an entry in docs/memory.md.
- Files < 500 lines. Pure functions in core; side effects at the edges.
- Comments say why, not what.
- Import types from '@core/types', never from individual type files.

## Process
- Read the file (and docs/memory.md) before editing it.
- Edit over create. No new docs unless asked.
- Root holds only conventional files. Code in src/, tests in tests/, docs in docs/.
- Never commit secrets or .env.
- Record architectural decisions in docs/memory.md with the reason.
- Update docs/TODO.md when a task is done.
